---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base
  title="Privacy — ChordPlane"
  description="What ChordPlane stores on your device, what a share link puts in the cloud, and what is never collected at all."
>
  <section class="wrap page-head">
    <h1>What ChordPlane does with your data</h1>
    <p>
      Short version: your library never leaves the device. The only thing that
      goes to a server is a sheet you explicitly share.
    </p>
    <p class="updated">Last updated 21 November 2026</p>
  </section>

  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="prose">
    <h2>On your device</h2>
    <p>
      Songs, set lists, transpose settings and preferences are stored in a local
      database inside the app. They are not uploaded, synced or backed up by
      ChordPlane. If you uninstall the app, Android removes that data with it.
    </p>

    <h2>If you create an account</h2>
    <p>
      An account is optional and only needed to create share links you can
      manage later. You can sign up with an email address and password, or with
      Google.
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Email and password:</strong> the address is stored by our
        authentication provider (Supabase). Passwords are hashed, never stored
        in readable form.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Google sign-in:</strong> Google tells us your email address,
        display name and profile picture URL. Nothing else is requested, and we
        do not receive access to Gmail, Drive or any other Google service.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>What a share link stores</h2>
    <p>
      Sharing is the one action that sends content to a server. When you share a
      song or a set list, ChordPlane stores:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>the sheet or set list you chose to share, as a fixed snapshot;</li>
      <li>your account's email address, so the share can be listed and removed;</li>
      <li>when it was created, and a random token that forms the link.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      <strong>A share link is public to anyone who has the URL.</strong> Treat it
      like posting the sheet: don't share material you don't have the right to
      distribute. Removing the share from the app deletes the stored snapshot,
      and the link stops working immediately.
    </p>

    <h2>Cookies and local storage</h2>
    <p>
      The app stores your sign-in session on the device so you stay logged in
      between launches. This website is static: it sets no advertising cookies
      and runs no analytics.
    </p>

    <h2>What is never collected</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>No analytics or usage tracking of any kind.</li>
      <li>No crash reporting or device identifiers.</li>
      <li>No advertising SDKs, and no data sold or shared with advertisers.</li>
      <li>No location, contacts, camera or microphone access.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Removing your data</h2>
    <p>
      Songs and set lists: delete them in the app, or uninstall it. Shares:
      remove them from <strong>My shares</strong> in the app. To delete your
      account entirely, including any shares still attached to it,
      <a href="https://github.com/danny192168/ChordPlane-v2/issues" rel="noopener"
        >open an issue</a
      >
      and it will be removed.
    </p>

    <h2>Children</h2>
    <p>
      ChordPlane is not directed at children under 13, and accounts are not
      knowingly created for them.
    </p>

    <h2>Changes</h2>
    <p>
      If this note changes in a way that affects what is stored, the date at the
      top changes with it.
    </p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>
      Questions about any of the above:
      <a href="https://github.com/danny192168/ChordPlane-v2/issues" rel="noopener"
        >open an issue on GitHub</a
      >.
    </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>
